0:["y07uMnhZvjRDJDyCaG9hS",[[["",{"children":["(workspace)",{"children":["learning",{"children":["strategy",{"children":[["id","contract-value-and-lot-size","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__?{\"id\":\"contract-value-and-lot-size\"}",{}]}]}]}]}]},"$undefined","$undefined",true],["",{"children":["(workspace)",{"children":["learning",{"children":["strategy",{"children":[["id","contract-value-and-lot-size","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__",{},[["$L1",["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-[820px] space-y-4 p-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/learning","className":"text-[11px] font-semibold text-teal hover:underline","children":"← All lessons"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2","children":[["$","h1",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-text","children":"Contract Value and Why Lot Sizes Change"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full px-2.5 py-0.5 text-[11px] font-bold leading-tight whitespace-nowrap bg-hover text-muted border border-border2 px-1.5 py-0 text-[9px]","children":"beginner"}],false]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-[12px] leading-relaxed text-muted","children":"SEBI fixes a notional contract-value band, not a lot size. Lot size is the dependent variable, recalculated as index levels drift — which is why every hardcoded lot size eventually goes stale."}]]}],false,["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-card border px-[18px] py-4 transition-colors duration-panel ease-standard bg-card border-border shadow-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-3 flex items-center gap-2","children":["$undefined",["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold leading-tight","children":["Lesson",false]}],false]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted [&_h1]:mb-2 [&_h1]:text-base [&_h1]:font-bold [&_h1]:text-text [&_h2]:mb-1.5 [&_h2]:mt-5 [&_h2]:text-[13px] [&_h2]:font-bold [&_h2]:text-text [&_h3]:mb-1 [&_h3]:mt-4 [&_h3]:text-[12px] [&_h3]:font-semibold [&_h3]:text-text [&_p]:mb-2.5 [&_strong]:font-semibold [&_strong]:text-text [&_ul]:mb-2.5 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_ol]:mb-2.5 [&_ol]:list-decimal [&_ol]:pl-5 [&_li]:mb-1 [&_code]:rounded [&_code]:bg-bg [&_code]:px-1 [&_code]:py-0.5 [&_code]:font-mono [&_code]:text-[11px] [&_code]:text-text [&_table]:mb-3 [&_table]:w-full [&_table]:text-left [&_table]:text-[11.5px] [&_th]:border-b [&_th]:border-border [&_th]:pb-1 [&_th]:pr-3 [&_th]:font-semibold [&_th]:text-text [&_td]:border-b [&_td]:border-border [&_td]:py-1 [&_td]:pr-3 [&_td]:align-top [&_a]:text-teal hover:[&_a]:underline [&_blockquote]:border-l-2 [&_blockquote]:border-border2 [&_blockquote]:pl-3 [&_blockquote]:italic","children":[["$","h1","h1-0",{"children":"Contract Value and Why Lot Sizes Change"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":["A recurring confusion in Indian derivatives is that lot sizes are a fixed\r\nproperty of an instrument. They are not. They are a ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"derived"}]," number,\r\nrecalculated by the exchange whenever the underlying's level moves far enough\r\nthat the contract's notional value leaves SEBI's prescribed band."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":"Understanding which variable is fixed and which is derived explains every lot\r\nsize revision that has happened and every one that will."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"children":"The relationship"}],"\n",["$","pre","pre-0",{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"children":"contract value  =  lot size  ×  underlying level\n"}]}],"\n",["$","p","p-2",{"children":["SEBI fixes ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"contract value"}],". The market determines the ",["$","strong","strong-1",{"children":"underlying level"}],".\r\nThe exchange solves for ",["$","strong","strong-2",{"children":"lot size"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":["Since November 2024, the minimum contract value for index derivatives is\r\n",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"₹15–20 lakh"}],", raised from the previous ₹5–10 lakh band."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-4",{"children":"So when an index rises substantially, its lot size is cut to bring the notional\r\nback within the band. When SEBI revises the band itself, every instrument's lot\r\nsize is recalculated at once. Both have happened."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"children":"Why this lesson states no numbers"}],"\n",["$","p","p-5",{"children":"No lesson in this folder states \"one NIFTY lot is N contracts\"."}],"\n",["$","p","p-6",{"children":"Lot sizes have been revised more than once in recent years — first by the\r\nNovember 2024 band increase, and again as index levels moved. Any figure\r\nwritten into prose here would be correct for a quarter or two and wrong\r\nthereafter, and wrong in a way that is invisible to a reader who has no reason\r\nto doubt it."}],"\n",["$","p","p-7",{"children":["The application handles this correctly already: live lot sizes are read from\r\nthe Dhan scrip master, which is the authoritative per-instrument source\r\n(",["$","span",null,{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"children":"scrip-master.service.ts"}]}],").\r\nThe Learning UI substitutes the live figure wherever a lesson needs one."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-8",{"children":["The general principle applies beyond lot sizes: ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"teach the mechanism, resolve\r\nthe number at runtime."}]," Margins are recomputed daily, statutory rates change\r\nby Finance Act, and expiry dates shift for holidays. Anything that a circular\r\ncan change does not belong in prose."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"children":"What changes when a lot size changes"}],"\n",["$","p","p-9",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Notional exposure per lot changes"}],", which is the point of the exercise. A\r\nposition sized in lots carries different exposure before and after a revision."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-10",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Strike steps do not change."}]," NIFTY strikes remain 50 apart, BANKNIFTY 100.\r\nSpread widths measured in strike steps are unaffected — which is why every\r\nstrategy lesson in this folder expresses strikes relatively (",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"ATM+2"}],") rather\r\nthan as absolute point distances."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-11",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Existing contracts are handled by the circular."}]," Revisions typically apply\r\nto new contracts from a stated date, with existing far-dated contracts adjusted\r\non a published schedule. Quarterly and half-yearly contracts have been revised\r\non different dates from monthlies."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-12",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Margin per lot changes"}],", since margin scales with notional."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-3",{"children":"The practical consequence for sizing"}],"\n",["$","p","p-13",{"children":["Because lot size falls as the index rises, the notional exposure of one lot is\r\nroughly stable ",["$","em","em-0",{"children":"by design"}],", within the band. This means:"]}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":["Position size in ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"lots"}]," is not a stable measure of risk across time or\r\nacross instruments."]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":["Position size in ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"notional rupees"}]," is."]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p","p-14",{"children":["A book holding \"two lots\" of two different indices holds two quite different\r\nexposures. A book sized against contract value holds what it intends to. This\r\nis the same argument that ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"risk/position-sizing.md"}]," makes from the risk side."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-4",{"children":"Related"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-1",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"india-market-structure/sebi-derivatives-framework.md"}]," — where the band comes from"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"risk/position-sizing.md"}]," — sizing against notional rather than lots or margin"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"india-market-structure/margins.md"}]," — what scales with notional"]}],"\n"]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[10px] leading-relaxed text-faint","children":["Educational material describing how a structure behaves. Not a recommendation, not a signal, and not personalised advice. Source: ",["$","code",null,{"className":"font-mono","children":"docs/learning/india-market-structure/contract-value-and-lot-size.md"}]]}]]}],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children","$4","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[[null,["$","$L6",null,{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateSty